window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-a1cb99fcde69be87"]={"key":"ny_c-a1cb99fcde69be87","group":"ny_c","uid":"a1cb99fcde69be87","rank":69,"title":"marchbank yewbank scar release package","occupation":"buyers_purchasing_agents","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c3","prompt":"You are Ilse Fitzgerald, the senior buyer at Marchbank Consortium responsible for releasing supplier corrective action requests, and Beatriz Coutinho needs the Yewbank Instruments weld-spatter SCAR out this week without creating a commercial concession or an unworkable demand. Kamil Ekstrom’s draft and the supporting incident, drawing, purchasing-term, response-time, and process-change information are all in `scar_release_source.xlsx`. The recurrence has become materially worse across the two periods shown there, but the draft currently states a root cause before Yewbank has investigated, demands a 100% sort at supplier cost without identifying authority for the charge, gives a containment date that has already passed, and says Marchbank has accepted the condition for years. Beatriz wants each damaged line visibly repaired and the reason for every change preserved for review. The underlying form also needs attention because its current completion fields allow a SCAR to be closed without evidence anyone can verify. Our SCAR administration is mid-change: email and the controlled log are still used during the transition, while the supplier portal becomes the system of record at the cutover described in the workbook. Open cases may straddle both practices, and the package must remain usable when a supplier cannot access the portal or a required response or verification cannot be obtained. Prepare `yewbank_scar_marked_up.docx`, showing the draft changes and their reasons in no more than six pages; `yewbank_scar_released.docx`, a clean issue-ready SCAR in no more than four pages; `marchbank_scar_template_revised.docx`, a reusable template with concise guidance for a buyer or quality coordinator who has never administered a SCAR, in no more than four pages; and `scar_release_decision_memo.docx`, a two-page maximum memorandum to Beatriz explaining the material period change, the significant revisions, and your release decision. Make any necessary judgment about the unsupported sort-cost language explicit in the memo and apply it consistently throughout the package. Close the memo with the release call, not a list of proposed next steps. Write all four files into the top level of the working directory using exactly those filenames.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/scar_release_source.xlsx` — Provides the draft SCAR, incident and period-comparison data, applicable drawing requirement and purchasing terms, response timing, current template content, approval context, and SCAR process-transition rules.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `yewbank_scar_marked_up.docx` — A visibly marked-up version of the draft SCAR that preserves each substantive change and its reasoning. (Maximum six rendered pages; changes and rationales must be reviewable without comparing against a separate undocumented draft.)\n- `yewbank_scar_released.docx` — A clean, issue-ready supplier corrective action request for Yewbank Instruments. (Maximum four rendered pages; all case facts and commitments must remain within the authority and evidence provided by the source workbook.)\n- `marchbank_scar_template_revised.docx` — A reusable SCAR template with concise completion guidance suitable for an inexperienced buyer or quality coordinator. (Maximum four rendered pages; must support both the transition period and portal end state, including blocked or incomplete cases.)\n- `scar_release_decision_memo.docx` — A decision memorandum to Beatriz Coutinho explaining the revisions, period change, commercial judgment, and release call. (Maximum two rendered pages; must end with an explicit release decision rather than a next-steps list.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/scar_release_source.xlsx","bytes":8311,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/1f382664b96df4a03c3fa18c0ac4f166864314a32ba1976e1336f200ec6bc576.xlsx","sha256":"1f382664b96df4a03c3fa18c0ac4f166864314a32ba1976e1336f200ec6bc576","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"SCAR Release Export","row_count":38,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Marchbank Consortium | Supplier Quality / Purchasing release export"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Exported 14-Mar-2026 16:42 UTC  |  CMQ-Log extract / attached source records"]},{"r":"4","cells":["CASE IDENTIFICATION","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["SCAR ID","MC-SCAR-26-041","","Status","Prepared for release",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["Supplier","Yewbank Instruments","","Supplier response role","Quality Manager",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Part / revision","74-1182 Mounting Collar / Rev D","","Intended issue date","46097",""]},{"r":"8","cells":["Recipient route","quality@yewbank-instruments.example","","Issuing role","Ilse Fitzgerald, Senior Buyer",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["Technical content review","Kamil Ekstrom, Supplier Quality Lead; reviewed 13-Mar-2026","","Supplier acknowledgement","Not yet received",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["Known traceability","Receipts R-88192, R-88317; YW-2601-04, YW-2601-11, YW-2602-03, YW-2602-07, YW-2602-12","","Locations noted","Marchbank receiving / line-side WIP / supplier finished goods pending confirmation",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["OBJECTIVE INCIDENT AND PERIOD RECORDS","","","","",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["Period","Received / inspected","Nonconforming","Affected lots","Evidence / dates","Location"]},{"r":"14","cells":["01-Oct-2025 to 31-Dec-2025","1240","11","2 of 18: YW-2510-08, YW-2511-02","IR-25-188 / 18-Nov-2025; receiving inspection","Marchbank receiving"]},{"r":"15","cells":["01-Jan-2026 to 29-Feb-2026","1060","47","5 of 14: YW-2601-04, YW-2601-11, YW-2602-03, YW-2602-07, YW-2602-12","IR-26-031 / 04-Feb-2026; IR-26-047 / 28-Feb-2026","Receiving and line-side WIP"]},{"r":"16","cells":["Latest incident detail","Receipt R-88317; lot YW-2602-12; 9 pieces found in receiving sample","","","28-Feb-2026","Receiving"]},{"r":"17","cells":["Observed condition","Weld spatter / raised residue observed on mounting interface face adjacent to locating bore.","","","Photo set IR-26-047-A through -D; inspection record attached to incident.",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["CONTROLLING REQUIREMENT","","","","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["Drawing","DWG 74-1182 Rev D, Note 6","","","",""]},{"r":"21","cells":["Drawing excerpt","Remove all weld spatter from the mounting interface face and locating bore. No raised residue is permitted on either interface feature.","","","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["PURCHASING / RESPONSE RULES","","","","",""]},{"r":"24","cells":["Purchasing Terms §12.4","Supplier shall cooperate with investigation, provide timely response, and implement customer-accepted corrective action. Terms do not state unilateral supplier-paid sorting authority or automatic chargeback.","","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["SQ Response Rule SQR-3","Acknowledgement within 2 business days of issue; containment plan and completion confirmation within 1 business day; full 8D response within 10 business days. Extension must be documented, approved by SCAR Administrator, and recorded in CMQ-Log. Closure follows Marchbank review.","","","",""]},{"r":"26","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"27","cells":["CURRENT DRAFT SCAR - EDITABLE TEXT","","","","",""]},{"r":"28","cells":["Draft problem statement","Yewbank operator poor torch angle and inadequate cleaning caused weld spatter on the mounting collar.","","","",""]},{"r":"29","cells":["Draft containment","Yewbank shall perform a 100% sort at supplier cost and provide containment by 07-Mar-2026.","","","",""]},{"r":"30","cells":["Draft history","Marchbank has accepted this weld-spatter condition for years.","","","",""]},{"r":"31","cells":["Draft recurrence statement","A recent incident shows the weld-spatter problem continues.","","","",""]},{"r":"32","cells":["Draft closure control","Close when supplier marks corrective action complete.","","","",""]},{"r":"33","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"34","cells":["CURRENT TEMPLATE CONTENT / PROCESS CHANGE","","","","",""]},{"r":"35","cells":["Current template completion fields","Containment complete [ ]; Root cause complete [ ]; Corrective action complete [ ]; SCAR closed [ ]. No evidence identifier, effectiveness result, reviewer, or review date is required.","","","",""]},{"r":"36","cells":["Process change notice PCN-SQ-26-02","Until 30-Apr-2026: email submission and CMQ-Log remain controlled records. Cutover 01-May-2026: Supplier Action Portal (SAPortal) is system of record. Open SCARs crossing cutover retain CMQ-Log references and are migrated/reconciled in SAPortal.","","","",""]},{"r":"37","cells":["Access/outage control","When supplier cannot access SAPortal, use email plus QF-17 Temporary Submission Record, enter status and escalation owner in CMQ-Log, and reconcile attachments and milestone references to SAPortal within 2 business days after access is restored. Missing response, unavailable evidence, overdue action, or unavailable verifier remains Open - Blocked; do not close.","","","",""]},{"r":"38","cells":["Local status / closure terms","Prepared for release; Open; Open - Blocked; Supplier submitted; Technical acceptance; Commercial review (if applicable); Effectiveness approved; Closed by Marchbank.","","","",""]},{"r":"39","cells":["","System note: Column F is not consistently populated in older extracts.","","","",""]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/marchbank_scar_template_revised.docx","bytes":40848,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/736976c772da8c345d4b49f8eb817bc21c904efb5df805e373239a34a7d968d0.docx","sha256":"736976c772da8c345d4b49f8eb817bc21c904efb5df805e373239a34a7d968d0","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"SUPPLIER CORRECTIVE ACTION REQUEST - CONTROLLED TEMPLATE\nFor buyer or quality coordinator use. Complete fields marked [Required]; keep unknown items Open or Open - Blocked, never infer them.\nA. Control, identity, and objective problem definition\nField / prompt\nRecord\n[Required] SCAR ID; status; issue date; issuing role\n____________________________________________\n[Required] Supplier; response contact / role; recipient route\n____________________________________________\n[Required] Part, revision, PO/receipt; governing requirement (drawing/spec note)\n____________________________________________\n[Required] Objective evidence ID(s): incident, inspection, photos, samples\n____________________________________________\n[Required] Factual problem statement: feature/location, observed condition, acceptance condition. Do not state a presumed cause here.\n____________________________________________\n[Required] Known and potential scope: lots/shipments, population/quantity, locations, traceability records; mark confirmation pending where unknown.\n____________________________________________\n\nB. Containment and controlled disposition\n[Required] State the requested protection of supplier stock, customer receiving, WIP and future shipments. Do not state supplier cost liability unless an identified authority authorizes it; otherwise record “cost allocation reserved / commercial review required.”\nContainment action / suspect disposition\nOwner\nRequested or committed date\nStatus\nCompleted date\nVerification evidence ID / verifier / date\nIdentify / segregate / inspect / shipment control / disposition: __________________\n________\n________\nOpen\n________\n____________________________\nTraceability review and quantity reconciliation: __________________\n________\n________\nOpen\n________\n____________________________\nKnown/new suspect material location and disposition: __________________\n________\n________\nOpen\n________\n____________________________\n\nC. Supplier analysis and corrective action\nAnalysis requirement\nSupplier response / evidence reference\nOccurrence cause - why the condition occurred\nMethod: __________  Cause ID: __________  evidence/attachment: __________________\nEscape/detection cause - why it was not prevented or detected\nMethod: __________  Cause ID: __________  evidence/attachment: __________________\nCorrective action linked to Cause ID / failure mode\nAction / owner / due date / status / actual completion: ______________________________\nImplementation evidence (not just “complete”)\nWork instruction, training, inspection, process/change record, photo, etc.: __________________  Verified by / date: __________\n\nD. Effectiveness validation and review gates\nEffectiveness control\nRecord\nMetric and baseline / comparison basis\n____________________________________________\nTarget or acceptance criterion; monitored sample or window\n____________________________________________\nResult / evidence reference\n____________________________________________\nSupplier reviewer / date; Marchbank technical reviewer / review date\n____________________________________________\nSupplier submitted | Technical acceptance | Commercial review (if applicable) | Effectiveness approved | Closed by Marchbank\nName / role / date / decision / record reference: ______________________________\n\nClosure gate [Required]: Closed by Marchbank may be selected only when containment record, cause analysis, action implementation evidence, effectiveness result, and named Marchbank reviewer/date are all recorded. A checkbox, supplier claim, or submission alone is not closure.\nE. Channel record, cutover, and blocked-case control\nMilestone\nDate\nChannel used\nCMQ-Log / SAPortal / email / QF-17 reference\nRecorded by\nIssue / acknowledgement / containment / full response / acceptance / closure\n______\nEmail + CMQ-Log until 30-Apr-2026; SAPortal from 01-May-2026\n__________________________________\n________\nOpen case at cutover\n______\nPreserve CMQ-Log reference; migrate/reconcile in SAPortal\n__________________________________\n________\n\nException path: For portal inaccessibility, missing supplier response, unavailable evidence, overdue action, or unavailable verifier, set status Open - Blocked; name an escalation owner and due follow-up; retain email plus QF-17 Temporary Submission Record in CMQ-Log; document the missing item and interim control. Reconcile attachments and milestone references to SAPortal within 2 business days after access is restored. Do not close while blocked.\nStatus cues: Prepared for release = approved to issue; Open = work underway; Open - Blocked = normal path unavailable and exception record active; Supplier submitted = awaiting Marchbank review; Technical acceptance / Commercial review / Effectiveness approved are separate gates; Closed by Marchbank = final authorized decision only.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/scar_release_decision_memo.docx","bytes":39526,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/04d2b07ef2aa6cfbe0d5408a6ebae9268cb7041ced34c2890e5ae6cb3864daca.docx","sha256":"04d2b07ef2aa6cfbe0d5408a6ebae9268cb7041ced34c2890e5ae6cb3864daca","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"DECISION MEMORANDUM\nTo: Beatriz Coutinho  |  From: Ilse Fitzgerald, Senior Buyer  |  16-Mar-2026\nSubject: MC-SCAR-26-041 - Yewbank Instruments weld-spatter release package\nMaterial recurrence\nThe controlled incident record moves from 11 nonconforming pieces of 1240 received/inspected (0.9%; 2 of 18 lots) in 01-Oct-2025 to 31-Dec-2025 to 47 of 1060 (4.4%; 5 of 14 lots) in 01-Jan-2026 to 29-Feb-2026. The count is 36 higher while population is -180; the rate is 5.0 times the earlier rate. This is a material worsening in recurrence and lot incidence, but it does not prove a process or operator cause.\nRelease repairs and commercial judgment\nThe marked-up copy visibly removes the draft’s assertion that poor torch angle and cleaning caused the condition. The released SCAR instead records the observed raised residue at the mounting interface face/locating bore and requires Yewbank to distinguish occurrence cause from escape/detection cause with supporting evidence. That preserves the actual requirement in DWG 74-1182 Rev D, Note 6.\nThe draft’s 100% sort “at supplier cost” is not supported by Purchasing Terms §12.4: it requires cooperation and accepted corrective action, but grants no unilateral sorting charge or automatic chargeback. I chose one treatment throughout the package: require controlled 100% inspection of suspect and future lots, lot-specific evidence, certification, segregation and documented disposition, while expressly reserving cost allocation for separate authorized commercial review. This protects product flow without inventing liability. The expired 07-Mar-2026 containment date is replaced by 17-Mar-2026, one business day after issue; acknowledgement and full response are 18-Mar-2026 and 30-Mar-2026 under SQR-3. Finally, the “accepted for years” line is removed. Prior detection records are retained only as recurrence evidence and expressly do not waive, deviate from, or alter the drawing.\nAdministration controls\nThe revised template separates requirement, objective evidence and factual problem; records containment, suspect scope/disposition, occurrence and escape analysis, cause-linked actions, implementation evidence, and measurable effectiveness review. It prevents a supplier completion box from closing a SCAR: named Marchbank review and evidence are required before Closed by Marchbank.\nDuring the transition, each milestone records channel and audit reference: email plus CMQ-Log through 30-Apr-2026, then SAPortal as system of record from 01-May-2026. Open cases retain CMQ-Log references through migration and reconciliation. For access failure, missing response/evidence, overdue action, or unavailable verification, the template requires Open - Blocked, an escalation owner, QF-17/email interim record, and reconciliation within two business days after access restoration. It preserves control instead of creating a silent stall or unsupported closure.\nRelease decision: release the corrected SCAR MC-SCAR-26-041 to Yewbank Instruments on 16-Mar-2026 with containment required by 17-Mar-2026, cost allocation expressly reserved pending authorized commercial review, and evidence-based Marchbank closure only.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/yewbank_scar_marked_up.docx","bytes":41110,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/80c0815eaa114dcd274d3c0c8af2c7ac88333e0999c3e545f6a196b7b431689a.docx","sha256":"80c0815eaa114dcd274d3c0c8af2c7ac88333e0999c3e545f6a196b7b431689a","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"SCAR RELEASE REVIEW - VISIBLE MARKUP\nMC-SCAR-26-041 | Yewbank Instruments | Review basis: scar_release_source.xlsx\nControl\nValue\nStatus\nPrepared for release - marked-up review copy\nPart\n74-1182 Mounting Collar / Rev D\nIssue / response route\n16-Mar-2026; email to quality@yewbank-instruments.example and CMQ-Log during current process\nReviewer / issuer\nKamil Ekstrom, Supplier Quality Lead; reviewed 13-Mar-2026 | Ilse Fitzgerald, Senior Buyer\n\nRed strike-through = deleted draft text. Green = replacement that will appear in the released SCAR. Blue reason column records the specific repair and source basis.\nLine-by-line release repairs\nDraft line\nDeleted wording\nReleased replacement\nReason / source basis\nProblem statement / presumed cause\nYewbank operator poor torch angle and inadequate cleaning caused weld spatter on the mounting collar.\nObserved condition: weld spatter / raised residue on the mounting interface face adjacent to the locating bore. Yewbank shall investigate and provide separately supported occurrence cause and escape/detection cause; no cause is established by this SCAR.\nThe incident records and photos establish condition, not torch angle or operator conduct. Separating occurrence from escape prevents an unsupported conclusion. Basis: IR-26-047; Drawing Note 6.\nContainment / cost\nYewbank shall perform a 100% sort at supplier cost and provide containment by 07-Mar-2026.\nBy 17-Mar-2026, identify, segregate and control-inspect known and potentially suspect material at Yewbank, Marchbank receiving and line-side WIP; report quantities, lots, locations and controlled disposition. Apply 100% inspection to suspect and future lots until Marchbank accepts corrective action or effectiveness is demonstrated; provide lot-specific inspection record and shipment certification. Cost allocation is expressly reserved pending separate authorized commercial review.\n07-Mar-2026 is before the intended issue date. SQR-3 requires containment within 1 business day. Terms §12.4 requires cooperation but does not authorize unilateral supplier-paid sorting or chargeback; containment need is retained and commercial allocation reserved.\nHistorical statement\nMarchbank has accepted this weld-spatter condition for years.\nPrior records show detections in two periods; they do not constitute acceptance, waiver, deviation approval, or a change to DWG 74-1182 Rev D Note 6. The drawing requirement remains controlling.\nDeletes implied concession that could waive the print. Basis: Drawing Note 6 and objective period/incident records.\nRecurrence evidence\nA recent incident shows the weld-spatter problem continues.\nComparable period record: 11/1240 (0.9%) across 2 of 18: YW-2510-08, YW-2511-02; later period 47/1060 (4.4%) across 5 of 14: YW-2601-04, YW-2601-11, YW-2602-03, YW-2602-07, YW-2602-12. Nonconforming count rose 36 and rate rose 5.0x; data do not establish cause.\nReplaces latest-incident-only characterization with both comparable periods, accurate counts/rates and lot incidence. Basis: objective incident record table.\nResponse milestones\nNo separate acknowledgement, cause, action, evidence, or effectiveness commitments.\nSupplier acknowledgement due 18-Mar-2026; full 8D response due 30-Mar-2026. Response must state occurrence and escape causes, analysis/evidence, cause-linked actions with owners/dates, implementation evidence, and proposed measurable effectiveness review. Extensions require documented SCAR Administrator approval and CMQ-Log entry.\nAdds the SQR-3 timing and the records required to verify a response; dates follow 2 and 10 business-day intervals from issue.\nClosure gate\nClose when supplier marks corrective action complete.\nSupplier submission does not close the SCAR. Marchbank may close only after authorized technical review confirms containment records, analysis, implementation evidence, and effectiveness evidence against an agreed metric/window; status and reviewer/date are recorded.\nCurrent template allows checkbox closure without evidence or reviewer. Repair protects evidence-based closure. Basis: current template content; SQR-3 closure rule.\nTransition / exception\nNo response channel, cutover record, or blocked-case handling stated.\nUntil 30-Apr-2026 submit by email and record in CMQ-Log. If still open at 01-May-2026, preserve CMQ-Log references and migrate/reconcile to SAPortal, the system of record. If portal access, response, evidence or verification is unavailable, retain Open - Blocked, assign escalation owner, use QF-17/email interim record, and reconcile within 2 business days after access restoration.\nMakes the form usable through PCN-SQ-26-02 cutover and prevents undocumented stall or false closure. Basis: process change and access/outage control.\n\nUnchanged controlled identification and observed scope\nSupplier: Yewbank Instruments. Part: 74-1182 Mounting Collar / Rev D. Known references: Receipts R-88192, R-88317; YW-2601-04, YW-2601-11, YW-2602-03, YW-2602-07, YW-2602-12. The known findings do not define the full suspect population; Yewbank must reconcile traceability, quantities, locations and disposition in its containment response.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/yewbank_scar_released.docx","bytes":40931,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/869a64f56685dbc86cfa5583c68a993f96a87da3b966bc4c55b57b3874421379.docx","sha256":"869a64f56685dbc86cfa5583c68a993f96a87da3b966bc4c55b57b3874421379","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"SUPPLIER CORRECTIVE ACTION REQUEST\nMC-SCAR-26-041  |  Status: Prepared for release  |  Issue date: 16-Mar-2026\nField\nControlled value\nSupplier / response role\nYewbank Instruments | Quality Manager (acknowledgement requested; not yet received)\nProduct / requirement\n74-1182 Mounting Collar / Rev D | DWG 74-1182 Rev D, Note 6: Remove all weld spatter from the mounting interface face and locating bore. No raised residue is permitted on either interface feature.\nRecipient / issuing authority\nquality@yewbank-instruments.example | Ilse Fitzgerald, Senior Buyer; technical content review: Kamil Ekstrom, Supplier Quality Lead; reviewed 13-Mar-2026\nKnown scope\nReceipts R-88192, R-88317; YW-2601-04, YW-2601-11, YW-2602-03, YW-2602-07, YW-2602-12. Known findings are not the full suspect population; supplier confirmation required.\nResponse route through 30-Apr-2026\nReply by email to the issuing route and identify MC-SCAR-26-041; Marchbank records milestones in CMQ-Log.\n\n1. Objective nonconformance and recurrence\nObserved condition: weld spatter / raised residue was observed on the mounting interface face adjacent to the locating bore. It does not meet the stated drawing note. Evidence: IR-25-188, IR-26-031, IR-26-047 and photo set IR-26-047-A through -D. This SCAR does not assign a cause or blame.\nComparable period\nReceived / inspected\nNonconforming\nRate\nAffected lots\n01-Oct-2025 to 31-Dec-2025\n1240\n11\n0.9%\n2 of 18: YW-2510-08, YW-2511-02\n01-Jan-2026 to 29-Feb-2026\n1060\n47\n4.4%\n5 of 14: YW-2601-04, YW-2601-11, YW-2602-03, YW-2602-07, YW-2602-12\n\nThe later period has 36 more nonconforming pieces despite -180 fewer received/inspected pieces, and the rate increased from 0.9% to 4.4% (5.0x). Lot incidence rose from 2 of 18 to 5 of 14. This makes recurrence material; the records do not establish why it changed.\n2. Immediate containment and suspect material\nBy 17-Mar-2026 (1 business day after issue), acknowledge this SCAR and provide a containment plan and completion confirmation. Identify, segregate and controlled-inspect known and potentially suspect material at Yewbank, Marchbank receiving, and Marchbank line-side WIP. Reconcile all suspect lots/shipments, quantities and locations; give each known or newly identified suspect population a documented status and controlled disposition (quarantine, rework, return, scrap, or approved concession review). Detection alone is not disposition.\nApply 100% inspection to the suspect population and all future shipments until Marchbank accepts corrective action or effectiveness is demonstrated. Each shipment must be controlled-identified and accompanied by lot-specific inspection evidence and a shipment certification confirming compliance with Drawing Note 6. This containment request does not authorize a supplier charge, chargeback, or cost allocation. Allocation of sorting or related cost is expressly reserved for separate authorized commercial review under Purchasing Terms §12.4.\n3. Supplier response and evidence\nAcknowledge receipt by 18-Mar-2026 (2 business days). Submit a complete 8D response by 30-Mar-2026 (10 business days): (a) occurrence cause, (b) escape/detection cause, (c) analysis method and supporting records, (d) cause-linked corrective actions with action owner, due date, status and actual completion date, and (e) implementation evidence identifiers (for example revised work instruction, training record, inspection record, process/change record or photographs). Any extension must be documented, approved by the SCAR Administrator, and recorded in CMQ-Log before the applicable due date.\n4. Effectiveness, rights, and closure\nFor each action, propose an effectiveness measure with baseline/comparison, acceptance criterion, monitored lots or observation window, result, and supplier reviewer/date. Marchbank will designate the technical reviewer and review timing after implementation evidence is received. Supplier submission or a completed action does not close this SCAR. Closure is reserved to authorized Marchbank review after containment, supported cause analysis, implementation evidence, and effectiveness evidence are available.\nNo prior detection history constitutes acceptance, waiver, permanent deviation, or a change to the drawing. Marchbank reserves all rights and requires the drawing requirement to be maintained. If this SCAR remains open at 01-May-2026, Marchbank will preserve CMQ-Log references and migrate/reconcile the case to SAPortal, the system of record. If portal access is unavailable, supplier shall use the email route; Marchbank will use QF-17 and maintain Open - Blocked with an escalation owner until reconciliation within 2 business days after access restoration.\nSupplier acknowledgement (requested)\nMarchbank closure control\nName / role: ____________________   Date: __________   Response reference: ____________________\nStatus: Prepared for release / Open / Open - Blocked / Supplier submitted / Technical acceptance / Commercial review (if applicable) / Effectiveness approved / Closed by Marchbank\nAuthorized Marchbank reviewer: ____________________   Review date: __________\n","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"`yewbank_scar_marked_up.docx` exists at the required location, is a valid DOCX, opens successfully, and contains reviewable content.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted marked-up SCAR file.","grader_hint":"Open the DOCX and confirm it is not corrupt, empty, or merely a link to another artifact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"`yewbank_scar_released.docx` exists at the required location, is a valid DOCX, opens successfully, and contains the clean SCAR.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted released SCAR file.","grader_hint":"Open the DOCX and confirm it contains a clean issue document rather than only commentary or markup."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"`marchbank_scar_template_revised.docx` exists at the required location, is a valid DOCX, opens successfully, and contains a reusable template.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted revised template file.","grader_hint":"Confirm the file is an editable DOCX with reusable fields or prompts rather than a completed copy of this case."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"`scar_release_decision_memo.docx` exists at the required location, is a valid DOCX, opens successfully, and contains the decision memorandum.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted decision memo file.","grader_hint":"Open the DOCX and confirm it is a substantive memorandum rather than a cover page or transmittal note."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The marked-up SCAR makes all four consequential draft defects readily identifiable: the premature root cause, unsupported supplier-paid sort, expired containment date, and historical-acceptance statement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible revisions and annotations in `yewbank_scar_marked_up.docx`.","grader_hint":"Accept native tracked changes, comments, or an unambiguous original/replacement annotation method. All four source lines must be locatable without guesswork."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The marked-up SCAR replaces the asserted root cause with neutral language that records the observed nonconformance and assigns investigation of occurrence and escape causes to the supplier.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Root-cause revision in the marked-up SCAR.","grader_hint":"The replacement should not attribute fault, torch angle, operator carelessness, or another cause as established before Yewbank investigates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The marked-up SCAR repairs the sort-and-cost demand using a defensible approach that protects containment needs without asserting unsupported charging authority.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sort/cost revision and rationale in the marked-up SCAR.","grader_hint":"Accept either a requested 100% inspection with cost allocation expressly reserved or an alternative containment structure using segregation, traceability, certification, and separate commercial authorization. Do not require one approach over the other."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The marked-up SCAR replaces the elapsed containment deadline with timing that is achievable from the intended issue date and agrees with the applicable response interval in the source.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Revised containment timing compared with issue timing and response rules in the source workbook.","grader_hint":"Check the date or relative interval against the intended release date, business-day convention, and local response rule. It must not already be past when issued."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The marked-up SCAR removes the historical-acceptance concession and replaces it with language that preserves the drawing requirement and avoids waiver or implied deviation approval.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Historical-acceptance revision and rationale in the marked-up SCAR.","grader_hint":"The replacement should distinguish prior detection history, if retained at all, from acceptance of nonconforming product."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Every substantive marked-up change has a specific reason explaining the quality, commercial, timing, evidentiary, or usability problem it fixes.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comments, rationale column, or equivalent annotations in the marked-up SCAR.","grader_hint":"Generic notes such as 'reworded' or 'clarified' do not earn full credit unless they identify the actual defect being repaired."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The marked-up rationales identify the relevant source basis for requirement, evidence, timing, or authority-sensitive changes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source references embedded in the marked-up SCAR.","grader_hint":"Look for usable references to the drawing note, incident evidence, purchasing term, response rule, or transition rule as applicable; exact cell addresses are unnecessary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The marked-up SCAR consistently distinguishes verified observations and records from supplier conclusions, assumptions, and actions still awaiting evidence.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Language choices and annotations throughout the marked-up SCAR.","grader_hint":"Review the whole document for disciplined labels such as observed, reported, requested, pending, and verified rather than treating all statements as established facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The marked-up SCAR incorporates the source-supported comparison of the two periods rather than characterizing recurrence solely from the latest incident.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period comparison added to or corrected in the marked-up SCAR.","grader_hint":"Confirm both source periods are represented and that the direction of change follows the workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The markup is operationally reviewable: retained text, deleted text, replacement text, and explanatory commentary cannot reasonably be confused with one another.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered marked-up SCAR.","grader_hint":"Judge the rendered document, including legends or visual conventions. Formatting alone must not obscure what will appear in the released version."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The released SCAR reproduces the correct supplier, part, revision, SCAR identifier, affected lots or traceability references, and intended issue context from the source.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Identification fields in the released SCAR compared with the workbook.","grader_hint":"Check each populated identifier against the source; do not award for plausible but invented values."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The released SCAR states the applicable product requirement accurately and cites the controlling drawing note or equivalent source designation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Requirement statement in the released SCAR and the supplied drawing excerpt.","grader_hint":"The wording may be paraphrased but must preserve the actual scope and acceptance condition of the supplied requirement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The nonconformance description is objective, locates the weld spatter on the relevant product feature, and separates the observed condition from any unproven mechanism or blame.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Problem description in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"A recipient should understand what failed and where without being told an unsupported root cause."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR defines the known and potentially suspect scope using available lot, date, shipment, inventory, or traceability information and identifies remaining scope confirmation as a supplier response obligation where necessary.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and traceability content in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"The SCAR should not silently equate inspected failures with the full suspect population."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The released SCAR's period volumes and nonconforming quantities equal the source values, and any calculated nonconformance rates are accurate to within ±0.1 percentage point.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period-comparison figures in the released SCAR and source workbook.","grader_hint":"Recalculate each displayed rate as the applicable nonconforming quantity divided by the corresponding inspected or received population defined in the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR explains the material period change in business-relevant terms, including both direction and magnitude, without claiming a cause that the data do not establish.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Trend or recurrence statement in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Look for more than 'increased'; the statement should convey scale through counts, rates, lots, or an accurate comparison while reserving causation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR requests immediate containment actions that protect Marchbank inventory, work in process, and future receipts while the supplier investigation is open.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Containment section of the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Suitable actions may include identification, segregation, controlled inspection, and protection of shipments. Judge whether the request addresses more than one location in the supply stream."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR requires a documented disposition or status for known and newly identified suspect material rather than treating detection alone as containment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Suspect-material handling requirements in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Look for quarantine, rework, return, concession review, scrap, or another controlled disposition with records."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR establishes a verifiable shipment-protection mechanism until corrective action is accepted or effectiveness is demonstrated.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Future-shipment controls in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Examples include shipment certification, lot-specific inspection evidence, controlled identification, or another auditable release control; a bare promise to improve is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR requests supplier acknowledgement and identifies a responsible supplier contact or role without fabricating an acknowledgement that has not yet occurred.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Acknowledgement and supplier-responsibility fields in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"A blank response field or explicit request is acceptable; a pre-completed supplier acceptance without source evidence is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The supplier response requirement separately addresses occurrence root cause and escape or detection failure and calls for evidence supporting the analysis.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Root-cause response requirements in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"The document should prevent a single unsupported cause statement from satisfying both why the defect occurred and why it was not prevented or detected."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR requires corrective actions to be linked to identified causes and assigned to owners and due dates.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrective-action response requirements in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Check that action accountability is explicit and that generic retraining alone is not implicitly accepted as sufficient regardless of the eventual cause."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All requested response and containment dates in the released SCAR are internally ordered, not earlier than issue, and consistent with the supplied business-day response rules or documented extension mechanism.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dates and timing language in the released SCAR compared with source timing rules.","grader_hint":"Check containment, acknowledgement, root-cause, corrective-action, and any extension timing as a coherent sequence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR specifies implementation evidence that must accompany claimed completion rather than permitting completion to be established by a yes/no status alone.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence requirements in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Suitable evidence may include revised work instructions, training records, inspection results, photographs, process records, or change records, depending on the eventual action."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR defines an effectiveness review with a measurable acceptance basis, observation window or sample, responsible reviewer, and review timing.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Effectiveness requirements in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"The exact metric may be proposed by the supplier, but the SCAR must require objective post-implementation verification rather than immediate closure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR reserves closure for authorized Marchbank review after required responses, implementation evidence, and effectiveness evidence are available.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closure language and approval fields in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Supplier completion or a submitted response must not automatically equal Marchbank closure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR applies one defensible and explicit treatment of the unsupported sort-cost issue without asserting that the supplied purchasing terms authorize unilateral supplier charging.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Containment, commercial-reservation, and authorization language in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Accept either permitted reading described in R07 if operationally complete. The critical distinction is between needed containment and unproven cost liability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR preserves Marchbank's rights and the drawing requirement without stating or implying that prior history constituted acceptance, waiver, permanent deviation, or a change to the print.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Requirement, history, reservation, and disposition language in the released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Review the document as a whole; a disclaimer does not cure contradictory language elsewhere."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The released SCAR is genuinely issue-ready: status, issuing organization or role, response route, issue timing, and recipient instructions are sufficiently complete for Yewbank to act without asking what the document requires.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered released SCAR.","grader_hint":"Do not require a fabricated handwritten signature. Assess whether the supplied authority and prepared release status are represented honestly and actionably."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template prompts separately for the governing requirement, objective evidence of nonconformance, and a factual problem statement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Problem-definition fields and guidance in the revised template.","grader_hint":"The template should discourage blending the requirement, symptom, and presumed root cause into one narrative box."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template captures supplier and product identity, part and revision, source requirement, affected records, and lot or shipment traceability needed to define scope.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Identification and scope fields in the revised template.","grader_hint":"Equivalent field labels are acceptable if an inexperienced user can tell what evidence belongs in each."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template records each containment action with an owner, requested or committed date, completion status, completion date, and verification evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Containment tracking portion of the revised template.","grader_hint":"A single open narrative field or completed checkbox does not satisfy the accountability and verification dimensions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template provides for suspect-population definition, traceability review, quantity or scope reconciliation, location, and controlled disposition.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and disposition prompts in the revised template.","grader_hint":"The template should support recording unknown scope as pending work rather than forcing an unsupported final quantity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template separately captures occurrence cause, escape or detection cause, analysis method, and supporting evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Root-cause analysis prompts in the revised template.","grader_hint":"Look for separation sufficient to prevent a single conclusory statement from closing root-cause analysis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template links corrective actions to the cause or failure mode each action is intended to address.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrective-action fields in the revised template.","grader_hint":"A cause identifier, action-to-cause mapping, or equally clear mechanism is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template captures an action owner, due date, actual completion date, and status for each corrective action.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action-accountability fields in the revised template.","grader_hint":"Confirm these are per-action controls rather than one overall SCAR owner and date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template requires references or attachments for implementation evidence and provides a way to identify who verified that evidence and when.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Implementation-evidence and verification prompts in the revised template.","grader_hint":"A generic attachment checkbox without evidence identity, verifier, and date is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template captures an effectiveness metric, baseline or comparison basis, target or acceptance criterion, sample or monitoring window, result, reviewer, and review date.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Effectiveness-validation fields in the revised template.","grader_hint":"Equivalent terminology is acceptable. All elements must be available so closure can be independently audited."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template distinguishes supplier submission, Marchbank technical acceptance, commercial review where applicable, effectiveness approval, and final closure decision.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Review and closure controls in the revised template.","grader_hint":"The exact role names may follow the source, but one undifferentiated approval box is not enough."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template prevents unverifiable closure by requiring identified evidence and reviewer confirmation before final closed status can be selected.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closure logic, instructions, and fields in the revised template.","grader_hint":"Judge the practical workflow created by the template, not merely whether it contains the word 'evidence'."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template records the submission and approval channel used for each relevant milestone so an open SCAR can straddle the controlled-log and portal practices without losing its audit trail.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition and channel-recording controls in the revised template.","grader_hint":"The mechanism should distinguish current-process records from portal records and support later reconciliation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template provides an executable exception path for portal inaccessibility, missing supplier response, unavailable evidence, overdue action, or unavailable verifier, including status, escalation owner, interim record, and reconciliation or follow-up.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception, escalation, and blocked-case guidance in the revised template.","grader_hint":"The template need not use these exact labels, but it must tell a novice how to preserve control when normal completion is impossible rather than allowing false closure or an undocumented stall."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The revised template includes concise completion guidance, status definitions, and document-control cues sufficient for a first-time buyer or quality coordinator to use it without asking the author how fields or gates work.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered revised template and embedded instructions.","grader_hint":"Judge usability for the stated novice reader. Guidance should be concise but must distinguish required entries, pending items, verification, and closure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The decision memo gives one explicit release call for the corrected SCAR and ends on that decision rather than an unresolved recommendation or a next-steps list.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conclusion and final text of the decision memo.","grader_hint":"The call may be release, release with clearly incorporated conditions, or hold if the source makes release impossible, but it must be singular, justified, and consistent with the submitted SCAR status."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The decision memo explains the reason for repairing each of the four harmful draft lines and accurately describes how the submitted package resolved each one.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision memo compared with both SCAR versions.","grader_hint":"Check premature causation, unsupported cost demand, expired date, and historical-acceptance concession individually."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The decision memo compares the two source periods using correct quantities and rates within ±0.1 percentage point and accurately explains why the change is material.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period discussion in the decision memo and source workbook.","grader_hint":"Recalculate displayed rates and confirm that the narrative direction and magnitude match the data."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The decision memo makes the chosen treatment of the sort-cost ambiguity explicit, explains its authority and operational rationale, and does not present the alternative as simultaneously controlling.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Commercial-judgment section of the decision memo.","grader_hint":"Accept either defensible reading: reserve cost while requesting controlled 100% inspection, or separate commercial authorization while requiring traceability-based containment. The choice must be deliberate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The decision memo explains how the revised template supports both the current controlled-log practice, the portal end state, and open SCARs spanning the cutover.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition discussion in the decision memo and controls in the revised template.","grader_hint":"The memo should identify the operational effect of the transition controls rather than merely announcing that a portal is coming."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The decision memo identifies what happens when normal SCAR administration cannot be completed and accurately reflects the escalation, interim-record, and follow-up controls built into the template.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception discussion in the decision memo and exception path in the revised template.","grader_hint":"Look for an actionable blocked-case treatment, not a statement that exceptions will be handled case by case."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Supplier identity, part and revision, source requirement, affected scope, period figures, response timing, containment approach, commercial reservation, process-transition treatment, and release status agree across all deliverables wherever repeated.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document comparison of the marked-up SCAR, released SCAR, revised template examples if any, and decision memo.","grader_hint":"Audit repeated case facts and conclusions. The reusable template may use placeholders, but any included case example must agree with the other files."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The marked-up SCAR is no more than six rendered pages, the released SCAR no more than four, the revised template no more than four, and the decision memo no more than two; all remain legible and professionally usable without clipped or overlapping content.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered versions of all four DOCX deliverables.","grader_hint":"Render each file using a standard office suite, count pages, and inspect tables, comments, headers, footers, and page breaks for clipping or unreadably compressed text."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Marchbank Consortium is preparing an enterprise supplier corrective action for a recurring weld-spatter nonconformance at Yewbank Instruments. Purchasing must convert a problematic quality draft into a commercially supportable release package while Marchbank changes its SCAR administration process.","difficulty_sources":["Separating objective nonconformance evidence from an unverified supplier root cause","Balancing immediate containment against unsupported supplier cost liability","Repairing language that could imply waiver of a drawing requirement","Reconciling two periods and communicating a material recurrence change accurately","Redesigning closure controls so implementation and effectiveness are independently verifiable","Supporting both a controlled-process transition and blocked-case exception handling","Maintaining consistency across four interdependent release artifacts"],"authoring_plan":{"reference_artifact":{"filename":"scar_release_source.xlsx","content_requirements":["Include the current draft SCAR as editable, clearly readable source content, together with its case identifiers, intended issue timing, recipient, product revision, affected traceability, and current status.","Include objective incident records for two comparable periods. Supply received or inspected populations, nonconforming quantities, affected lots, locations, and dates so counts and rates can be reconciled and a materially worsening recurrence can be demonstrated without implying causation.","Include the controlling drawing excerpt with a designated note requiring removal of weld spatter and prohibiting raised residue on the affected mounting or interface feature.","Include a purchasing-term excerpt that requires supplier cooperation, investigation, response, and implementation of accepted corrective action but does not authorize unilateral supplier-paid sorting or automatic chargeback.","Include a supplier-quality response rule that defines containment and full-response intervals in business days from issue, allows documented extensions, and makes closure dependent on customer review.","Include the current SCAR template content, which permits closure through broad completion fields or checkboxes without separately capturing implementation evidence, effectiveness evidence, reviewer identity, or review date.","Include a controlled process-change notice defining the current email and controlled-log practice, the portal cutover date, the portal end state, treatment of open cases spanning cutover, and the approved outage or access-failure record and reconciliation expectations.","Include source-backed approval context sufficient for the purchasing role to prepare and release a corrected SCAR without fabricating a supplier acknowledgement or another person's signature.","Carry the exact local labels or vocabulary expected in outputs, including the SCAR identifier format, status terms, response milestone names, current controlled-log name, portal name, and closure decision terminology."]},"seeded_draft_imperfections":["The draft asserts a specific process or operator root cause even though the evidence establishes only the product condition and recurrence.","The draft demands 100% sorting at supplier cost but cites no contractual, purchase-order, policy, or approved commercial authority for cost allocation.","The draft gives an absolute containment deadline that precedes the intended issue date.","The draft states that the customer has accepted the weld-spatter condition for years, creating an implied waiver or deviation from the supplied drawing requirement.","The draft underuses the period evidence, allowing the latest incident to obscure the scale and direction of recurrence.","The current template uses completion-oriented fields that do not force links among cause, action, implementation evidence, effectiveness evidence, review, and closure."],"gold_relationships":["Every quantity reproduced in a deliverable must equal the corresponding source record. Each displayed nonconformance rate equals the applicable nonconforming quantity divided by the corresponding source population and should be rounded consistently.","The explanation of material change must compare both periods and accurately reflect changes in rate, count, lot incidence, or another supplied comparable measure without attributing the change to an unsupported cause.","Every requested date must be on or after issue and follow the supplied business-day intervals unless an extension is explicitly routed through the supplied approval mechanism.","The clean SCAR must preserve the drawing requirement and describe observed weld spatter objectively while leaving occurrence and escape causes for supplier investigation.","Containment must address known stock, work in process where relevant, suspect material, and future shipments, and must create evidence that Marchbank can verify.","One of two interpretations of the sort-cost tension is acceptable. The solver may request controlled 100% inspection while expressly reserving cost allocation pending authority, or may require segregation, traceability, certification, and a separately authorized commercial decision on sorting. Neither interpretation may assert unsupported supplier liability.","Prior detection or history cannot be written as acceptance, deviation approval, waiver, or print change. Any historical reference must preserve Marchbank's rights and distinguish non-detection or inconsistent enforcement from authorized acceptance.","Supplier response requirements must distinguish occurrence cause from escape or detection cause and link corrective actions to the causes they address.","Completion evidence and effectiveness evidence are different. Implementation records prove an action occurred; a defined metric, baseline or comparison, acceptance criterion, sample or window, result, reviewer, and date establish effectiveness.","Final closure belongs to an authorized Marchbank review after containment, cause analysis, corrective-action implementation, and effectiveness evidence are available; supplier submission alone cannot close the SCAR.","During transition, each milestone must retain its submission or approval channel and audit reference. Open cases spanning cutover must remain traceable across the controlled log and portal.","When the normal path is blocked by access failure, nonresponse, unavailable evidence, overdue action, or unavailable verification, the template must preserve an open or blocked status, identify an escalation owner, retain a controlled interim record, and require reconciliation or follow-up rather than allowing unsupported closure.","The decision memo, clean SCAR, markup, and any populated examples in the reusable template must agree on facts, timing, commercial treatment, transition handling, and release status."],"reference_solution_behavior":{"intended_verdict":"Release the corrected SCAR using one explicit and supportable treatment of the sort-cost ambiguity, with no fabricated supplier response or unsupported contractual claim.","markup_expectation":"The reference solution should use either native revision markup or a clear original/replacement/reason convention that visibly repairs each consequential line and cites the relevant source basis.","released_scar_expectation":"The clean SCAR should be supplier-facing, factual, issue-ready, measurable, and commercially reserved where the source does not grant charging authority.","template_expectation":"The revised template should be reusable rather than case-specific and should make evidence-based closure, transition handling, and exception handling executable for a novice administrator.","memo_expectation":"The memo should compare the source periods, justify the four key repairs, declare the chosen commercial interpretation, explain transition and blocked-case controls, and end with the release call."},"offline_validation":["Construct the workbook and all gold deliverables using Python and standard spreadsheet and word-processing libraries, then render the DOCX files with an offline office suite.","Recalculate all period metrics from the workbook, audit all response dates against the issue date and business-day rules, and compare repeated facts across the package.","Confirm that a solution using either acceptable sort-cost interpretation can earn full credit if applied consistently.","Verify rendered page limits, legibility, table integrity, visible markup, and the usability of the revised template for a first-time administrator.","Walk every rubric item using only the supplied workbook and submitted deliverables; no internet or unavailable private convention may be needed."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"scar_release_source","filename":"scar_release_source.xlsx","purpose":"Provides the draft SCAR, incident and period-comparison data, applicable drawing requirement and purchasing terms, response timing, current template content, approval context, and SCAR process-transition rules.","required":true,"discovery":"Review the workbook as the single controlled source for the case facts, local terminology, dates, authorities, and transition requirements."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"marked_up_scar","filename":"yewbank_scar_marked_up.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A visibly marked-up version of the draft SCAR that preserves each substantive change and its reasoning.","required":true,"constraints":["Maximum six rendered pages; changes and rationales must be reviewable without comparing against a separate undocumented draft."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"released_scar","filename":"yewbank_scar_released.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A clean, issue-ready supplier corrective action request for Yewbank Instruments.","required":true,"constraints":["Maximum four rendered pages; all case facts and commitments must remain within the authority and evidence provided by the source workbook."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"revised_template","filename":"marchbank_scar_template_revised.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A reusable SCAR template with concise completion guidance suitable for an inexperienced buyer or quality coordinator.","required":true,"constraints":["Maximum four rendered pages; must support both the transition period and portal end state, including blocked or incomplete cases."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"decision_memo","filename":"scar_release_decision_memo.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A decision memorandum to Beatriz Coutinho explaining the revisions, period change, commercial judgment, and release call.","required":true,"constraints":["Maximum two rendered pages; must end with an explicit release decision rather than a next-steps list."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"buyers_purchasing_agents","sector":"manufacturing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":7.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"A manufacturing supplier-quality practitioner should verify technical containment, investigation, effectiveness, and closure controls, while a purchasing or commercial reviewer independently checks authority-sensitive language, transition controls, and package consistency. Both reviewers should render all files and walk the rubric against the submitted artifacts and source workbook.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["More than one visual markup convention and more than one defensible treatment of the unsupported sort-cost demand are acceptable. Reviewers must assess whether the chosen approach is explicit, supportable, operationally complete, and consistent rather than requiring a single preferred wording."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:20+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:20+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:20+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:20+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:20+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c3/runs/a1cb99fcde69be87","declared_deliverables":["yewbank_scar_marked_up.docx","yewbank_scar_released.docx","marchbank_scar_template_revised.docx","scar_release_decision_memo.docx"]};
